# card7 = card6 with a row dropped when it has nothing (Albert, Nov 17 07:26: "If there is no spawning we don't need a green line"). opt.drop 'under': the one row sits under the bar; 'place': each row keeps its own place (green under the bar, blue at the bottom). The bar never moves.
# card6 = card5 with a send-a-villager ring in the bar for buildings a villager works (opt.vil; the Field tick), and a tighter sheet
# card5 = card4 with Demolish as tap, red fill, tap again (Albert, Nov 17 07:15): no word and no bar change; opt.armed draws the armed icon. The game's villager Controller already arms its Exit dot this way.
# card4 = card3 with no back mark anywhere and close as an X in a ring (Albert, Nov 17 07:04). With a cell selected the X steps back to the building's bar; with nothing selected it closes the card (Claude's call for back's old job).
# card3 = card2 with Repair and Demolish as two ringed icons in the bar (Albert, Nov 17 06:50: "why can't repair and demolish just be icons... a circle"), shown with the building's name and tabs; they give way to the reading line when a cell is selected. opt.icons turns it on.
# The static-footprint card, general: any building of n65 laid into the Jobs dock's two rectangles (bar 44, box 90). Claude's proposal after the run of Nov 17 06:21.
